<title>USA: Manufactured Home buys Western community.</title>
<headline>Manufactured Home buys Western community.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Manufactured Home Communities Inc said Friday it paid $23.3 million to acquire California Hawaiian Mobile Estates, a manufactured home community in San Jose, Calif.</p>
<p>The community consists of 412 sites on 50 acres situated around four lakes, Manufactured Home said.</p>
<p>The deal gives Manufactured Home 1,290 sites in northern California and ownership or controlling interests in 70 communities in 19 states.</p>
<p>The company's shares were off 1/8 Friday at 22-1/2.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
